WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.450
A painter's recipe card for green:
three parts blue to two parts yellow.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.520
There are eight litres of blue in the tin,

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.210
and plenty of yellow.

4
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.870
Use all the blue.

5
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.980
How much green paint can you make?

6
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.950
Is it just eight plus two?

7
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.370
In this mission, you'll see what a
ratio like three to two really means:

8
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.190
it compares parts, not litres.

9
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.200
You'll see that the eight litres
of blue fill all three blue parts,

10
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.280
so each part is equal.

11
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:32.670
And you'll find the size of one part,
then use it to build the whole mix.

12
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.250
Your mission: work out how much paint
you can make from eight litres of blue.
